<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Datasets</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following datasets are used and evaluated according to their respective benchmarks, found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Taori et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Longpre et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2018)</a></cite>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SST<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>5</span>.
Movie<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>review sentences annotated with five sentiment levels.
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Sentence: &lt;s&gt; - What is the sentiment?</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QQP</span>.
Pairs of Quora questions labelled as duplicates or not.
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Q1: &lt;q1&gt;\nQ2: &lt;q2&gt; - Duplicate? Yes/No</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> accuracy and F1.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RTE</span>.
Premise–hypothesis pairs drawn from news and Wikipedia, framed as binary entailment.
<span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Premise: &lt;p&gt; Hypothesis: &lt;h&gt; - Entailed? Yes/No</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">WANLI</span>.
Large<span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>scale adversarial Natural Language Inference corpus generated via human–AI collaboration.
<span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Premise: , Hypothesis:, Label: entail / neutral / contradict</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SQuAD v2</span>.
Wikipedia paragraphs paired with questions, mixing answerable and unanswerable cases.
<span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Context: &lt;para&gt; Question: &lt;q&gt; Answer:</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> exact match (EM) and F1.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HellaSwag</span>.
Multiple<span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>choice commonsense completion task built from WikiHow and activity narratives.
<span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Story: &lt;ctx&gt; Which ending (A–D) is most plausible?</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> multiple<span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>choice accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PubMedQA<span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>L</span>.
Biomedical abstracts with yes/no/maybe answers to research questions.
<span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Abstract: &lt;abs&gt; Question: &lt;q&gt; Answer (yes/no/maybe):</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">XSum</span>.
BBC news articles paired with single<span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>sentence abstractive summaries.
<span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Article: &lt;doc&gt; nWrite a one<span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>sentence summary:</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> ROUGE<span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>1/2/L.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CNN/DailyMail</span>.
Long<span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>form news articles with multi<span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>sentence “highlights”.
<span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Article: &lt;doc&gt; Summarise concisely:</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> ROUGE<span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>1/2/L.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alpaca<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>52k</span>.
GPT<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>3.5<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>generated instruction–response pairs covering diverse tasks.
<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Instruction: , Input: , Response:</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> GPT<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>4 preference win<span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text">-</span>rate.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FLANv2</span>.
Composite collection of <math id="A1.I1.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>1.8k tasks (12M examples) in instruction format.
<span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Template:</span> <span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Instruction: {task}Input: {x} Answer:</span>.
<span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric:</span> task<span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>specific (Accuracy, F1, ROUGE, etc.).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>N-gram Regularisation Loss</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To incorporate <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram regularisation into the standard causal language modelling loss function, we modify the loss function to include a penalty term that discourages the model from assigning excessively high confidence to certain <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-grams compared to the pre-trained model. The modified loss function consists of two main components:
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Primary Loss Term</span>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{LM}}=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p_{\theta}(x_{t}\mid x_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>LM</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{LM}}=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p_{\theta}(x_{t}\mid x_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the total length of the token sequence, <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token at position <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{&lt;t}=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{&lt;t}=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> represents all previous tokens before position <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(x_{t}\mid x_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(x_{t}\mid x_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of token <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> given previous tokens under the current model parameters <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the standard cross-entropy loss used for causal LLM training.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">N-gram Regularisation Term</span>:

<br class="ltx_break"></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}}=\lambda\sum_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\bigl[\max\{0,\;p_{\theta}(g)-p_{\theta_{0}}(g)-\tau\}\bigr]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>reg</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}}=\lambda\sum_{g\in\mathcal{G}}\bigl[\max\{0,\;p_{\theta}(g)-p_{\theta_{0}}(g)-\tau\}\bigr]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(g)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability assigned by the fine-tuned model to the <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{0}}(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{0}}(g)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability assigned by the pre-trained model to the same <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram, <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the regularisation strength, and <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the confidence margin. For an <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=(w_{1},\dots,w_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=(w_{1},\dots,w_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> we compute <math id="A2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(g)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}p_{\theta}(w_{i}\mid w_{&lt;i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(g)=\prod_{i=1}^{n}p_{\theta}(w_{i}\mid w_{&lt;i})</annotation></semantics></math> and analogously for <math id="A2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta_{0}}(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta_{0}}(g)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The penalty is applied only when the fine<span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>tuned model’s confidence exceeds the pre<span id="A2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>trained model’s by more than <math id="A2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise the term is zero. Balancing this term prevents the model from over<span id="A2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>memorising while preserving latent pre<span id="A2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>trained performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Qualitative Examples</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix C Qualitative Examples ‣ Early Detection and Reduction of Memorisation for Domain Adaptation and Instruction Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> contains example model output prefix-suffix pairs evaluated as ‘memorised’, alongside any incorrect continuations relative to ground truth.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T3.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T3.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Category</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A3.T3.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T3.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Input prefix, predicted suffix, and ground truth</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T3.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Instruction</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#606060;">Sophie sat at her desk, staring blankly at the computer</span><span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">screen. Her mind was racing as she weighed the options</span><span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">before deciding to quit her job.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;"></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[GT: in front of her.]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Review</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#606060;">Feels as if there’s a choke leash around your neck</span><span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">so director Nick Cassavetes can give it a good, hard yank</span><span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.4.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">and the audience grows impatient.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;"></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[GT: whenever he wants you to feel something.”]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Question</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#606060;">How can I lose ten pounds in three weeks without</span><span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">exercising? I currently weigh 185 pounds and have an office job</span><span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.6.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">that requires a lot of sitting.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;"></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[GT: but I dislike counting calories—what should I do?”]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">News</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#606060;">An American woman died aboard the MS Veendam, owned by</span><span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">cruise operator Holland America Line, after the ship docked in Rio de Janeiro</span><span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.8.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#990000;">, officials later added she was travelling alone.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;"></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">[GT: on Tuesday, according to the state-run Brazilian news agency Agencia Brasil.”]</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.10.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:45.5pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Medical</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#606060;">Oral gentamicin as well as oral and intraperitoneal polymyxin B,</span><span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#006400;">which binds endotoxin, did not prevent hepatic injury in rats with self<span id="A3.T3.3.10.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>filling blind loops.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T3.3.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T3.3.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;"></td>
<td id="A3.T3.3.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 6.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T3.3.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:150.8pt;">
